# FundamentalOS: config dir for the Play Integrity attestation forge. keystore2 reads the keybox +
# target-uid list here; the Settings integrity UI (system uid) AND the FundamentalForge fetch service
# (its own priv-app uid, fundamental_forge_app domain) both write them. Mode 0773 so a non-system uid
# can create files here; SELinux (fundamental_data_file, allowed only to keystore/system_app/
# fundamental_forge_app) is the real access boundary. chmod re-applies the mode to a dir that already
# exists from an earlier build.
on post-fs-data
    mkdir /data/misc/fundamental 0773 system system
    chmod 0773 /data/misc/fundamental
